# rbs's StringScanner#scan/#skip still type only Regexp patterns, predating Ruby
# 3.4's String-pattern support; rush passes single-char String literals (rubocop's
# Style/RedundantRegexpArgument prefers them). `| ...` appends the String overloads
# to the stdlib definitions — a plain redefinition would raise
# RBS::DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError, which Steep 2.0 does not surface: it
# silently drops the whole class to untyped (every StringScanner call stops being
# type-checked; measured via rush-211.5.12's untyped dump).
class StringScanner
  def scan: (String pattern) -> String?
          | ...

  def skip: (String pattern) -> Integer?
          | ...
end
